                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "std::all_of is being used for control flow and resource management rather than for expressing a logical \"all elements satisfy a predicate\" check.\n\nCan we use std:find_if?\nauto objectList = getFieldOIDList();\n\nauto failed = std::find_if(\n    objectList.begin(), objectList.end(),\n    [&](const auto& object) {\n        if (addPDUVar(*pdu, object.oid, object.oid_len,\n                      object.type, object.value))\n        {\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        lg2::error(\n            \"Failed to add SNMP var (type={TYPE}) for manager {SNMPMANAGER}\",\n            \"TYPE\", object.type, \"SNMPMANAGER\", mgr);\n        return true;\n    });\n\nif (failed != objectList.end())\n{\n    snmp_free_pdu(pdu);\n}"
                },
